All four fixes are in. `npm test` passes: worker vitest 47/47 in 7 files (was 45 in 6) and extension tests 38/38 (was 36). `npm run typecheck` is also clean.

**Files changed**
- **`worker/src/ingest.ts`**: when an incoming page has the same content hash as the stored one, ingest now checks whether the page has any chunk rows. If it has none, it calls `writeChunks`, so a page left without chunks by a failed request gets them on the retry. Otherwise it behaves as before (`merged`, 0 chunks).
- **`worker/test/ingest.test.ts`** (new): no existing worker test file covered ingest, so I added this one with a small in-memory D1 stand-in. Its first case makes the chunk write fail on the first request, then checks that the retry returns `merged` with chunks written. Its second case checks that a normal repeat visit still writes 0 chunks.
- **`extension/lib/blocklist.js`**: added a "# Cloud consoles" section with `console.aws.amazon.com`, `portal.azure.com` and `console.cloud.google.com`. A plain host entry blocks that host and its subdomains, so regional AWS consoles like `us-east-1.console.aws.amazon.com` are blocked too. Docs sites like `aws.amazon.com` and `cloud.google.com` are still captured. GitLab and Bitbucket were not added.
- **`extension/lib/redact.js`**: the regex now also matches the secret names when an underscore comes before them (`_SECRET`, `_TOKEN`, `_PASSWORD`), and adds `_KEY`. A bare word "key" without an underscore still isn't treated as a secret name, so prose like `primary key: ...` is left alone. One behaviour to know: in `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=value`, only `_KEY=value` is replaced, which leaves `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS[redacted-secret]`. The value is gone, and the test asserts this.
- **`extension/test/privacy.test.mjs`**: added a redaction test for `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=`, `API_TOKEN="..."`, `DB_PASSWORD:`, `MY_SECRET=` and the plain-"key" case. Also added a blocklist test for the three consoles and the two docs sites.
- **`.gitignore`**: added `!docs/kiro-logs/*.log` right after `*.log`.

